00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.391
So today, we're gonna meet up 

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.027
with an old-school Italian-American

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.662
Rich Mancuso

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.799
who's going to bring us into his nostalgic lens

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.033
of New York City

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.935
We're gonna go through his history here

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.570
What he's seen

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.072
but also get his take on

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:16.476
what things are currently like here in 2021

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.656
Have a good one

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.091
Yeah, you too, good luck with everything

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.695
Oh, man

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.864
It's the best, you know, I mean, really good Italian

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.599
regular Italian food

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.400
but like the bread bakeries

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.869
you can't find better bread anywhere

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:16.736
Alright

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.871
So have fun

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.938
Thank you

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:19.706
Rich!

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.074
How are you doing?

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.476
We're shaking, we're doing this

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.110
what do you want?

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.746
Ahh I don't know, I don't give a s**t anymore

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.115
Let me show you this first

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.917
Alright, we're in

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.286
Rich, say hi

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.522
Take this mask off first

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.057
Don't have to wear it outside

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.393
just have to wear it when we go somewhere indoors

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.128
So, this was all Italian back in the day?

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.197
Yeah, yeah, basically

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.966
In fact, I'm gonna show you now “The Bronx Tale”

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:47.433
Okay

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.003
Everyone knows the movie, here's the mural

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.437
What's the movie?

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.272
"Bronx Tale”

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.907
God, I haven't seen it

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:54.707
Oh, wow

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.842
Do I need to go home now?

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.210
Watch it and come back?

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.013
You need to see it because everyone has seen it

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.982
Based on this neighborhood back in the 60s

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:06.286
when there was the racial division

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.121
They didn't want any Blacks and Latinos

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.756
in the neighborhood

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.759
And the "Bronx Tale” is based on that a lot

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.561
and about the mob guys that 

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.195
tried to keep the neighborhood safe

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.931
Here's a mural of it right here on the wall

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.898
Alright

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.199
You might wanna see that

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.302
They just put this up a few years ago

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:25.338
When you think of Italians in New York

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.573
you think of... I mean

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.207
the tourist think of Little Italy

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:29.309
but this was it, right?

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:33.179
This was known as Little Italy, it still is

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.581
Little Italy, the Bronx

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.282
We're very far from Manhattan

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:36.816
Yeah

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:39.419
Mulberry Street’s little Italy of New York

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.254
but this is Little Italy of the Bronx

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.290
At one time, this community was designated

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.893
by the FBI as the safest

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.328
neighborhood in New York City

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:49.295
How's it now?

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.063
No

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.097
Okay

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:54.634
Unfortunate. And I'm not...

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.937
I'm not gonna fault anyone

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:01.174
But to tell you that when I grew up here 

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.842
on these streets

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.545
here and what we're gonna see

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.547
the mob influenced, the mob guys

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.915
Really?

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.383
Kept it safe

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.819
It was the mob keeping it safe, not the cops?

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:13.786
Yeah because

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.789
The cops were a part of it

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.825
They worked with them, they worked with the community

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.326
We had a beat cop

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:20.994
Ahh

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.428
You don't have that no more

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.631
We had one cop or two

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.798
They knew the whole neighborhood

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.635
walked around with the billy club

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:30.436
and when you that cop, you ran away

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.071
cus you didn't know

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.240
Let's just say, you have a business

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.210
Everyone of these shops was paying to the Italian mob?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.378
No

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.512
Didn't work that way

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:40.246
How'd it work?

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:41.314
See, that's a misconception

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:45.451
They did not control businesses and people

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:48.321
They were very kind-hearted people

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:51.090
that helped the community

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.925
Not like what you saw in "The Sopranos"

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.662
with Tony Soprano and them making sure that

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:57.163
that they controled the businesses

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.164
took the rent or whatever

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.400
Nah, that's not what it was like here

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.535
That's a misconception

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:05.471
What what they did was

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.940
protect the community

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.276
They helped people

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.445
They made sure these streets were safe

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.414
And as a result, when they were put away

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:17.317
and the cops couldn't control

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.319
Then the landlords took over these buildings

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.654
on section 8 and this neighborhood changed

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.090
So, how are they making their money then?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.827
They did things that weren't legal, we know that

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:30.296
So, were they selling drugs or?

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:33.766
When I was around them, I didn't see that

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:34.667
Okay

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:39.138
All of that might be going on, I never saw it

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:42.341
There was the illegal racket game of numbers

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:45.611
Gambling which now is not an issue at all

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.313
because it's all legal now

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:52.118
This is the main street 187th

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:55.021
And you'll still see the Italian presence

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.723
with the pastry shops

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.658
Oh yeah, the old-school pastry place?

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.693
And there still places that

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.395
were in here when I grew up

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.796
There's a little over there

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.232
Artuso, which was the most popular one

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.300
down the block

