00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:08.154
maybe cus I'm involved in sports all my life 

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.056
but never had any hate

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:13.059
or never bias toward some group over another

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:15.394
Yes, I'm an Italian

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:18.397
and I'm very proud of my heritage

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:21.000
An Italian American and I always will be

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.567
Yeah

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.769
And I also feel coming out of this neighborhood

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:27.940
that Italians don't get the credit they rightfully deserve

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.543
Contributing so much to society

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:33.312
in every walk of fashion of life

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:36.949
From the arts, to culture, to the food

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:40.653
to inventions, I mean, Enrico Fernmi, this one, that one

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:42.522
even Christopher Columbus

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:43.623
and now we got Christopher Columbus

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:44.790
that's under attack

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.792
This is what I love about your generation

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.528
that we're starting to lose a bit

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:51.063
I'm not young either but

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.965
this authenticity you know

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:54.867
this love for craft and

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:58.538
like mom and pop type shop it's sort of going away

00:08:58.538 --> 00:08:59.939
You don't have it today

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:03.876
The young people today in the Bronx, in the city

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:07.547
that's everywhere but here

00:09:07.547 --> 00:09:10.082
they would not know what we did

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.450
and what we went through

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.718
Times weren't easy

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.186
What do you mean by that?

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:17.089
You're saying it's not as good now, right?

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:18.224
You're saying like it's going downhill?

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:20.426
It wasn't great back then either

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:23.296
But the one thing that was great is we had

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:24.597
a stable household

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:26.899
a mother, a father

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.535
Today, that don't exist

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:31.504
Well, that's just for half the people, right?

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:33.439
I've worked with kids all my life

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:35.408
and I see it more and more

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:38.411
A lot of young people don't know who their real mom is

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:41.514
or also who their little dad is

00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:42.114
Yeah

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.483
We always had that structure in my house

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:46.319
and most of people in this community knew

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:47.720
who their mom and dad was

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.623
who their brother and sister was

00:09:50.623 --> 00:09:52.658
And that contributed a lot to

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:54.927
making this neighborhood strong

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:58.698
because if there was a problem...

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:00.299
If a merchant knew you did something wrong

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:02.001
they knew your mom or dad

00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:04.403
If a cop knew, a beat cop knew something’s wrong

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.705
they knew your mom or dad

00:10:05.705 --> 00:10:07.506
And it wasn't fun to deal with mom and dad

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:08.341
No, no

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:10.076
Not in my house!

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:12.044
I have an Italian-American father

00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:14.347
He was hard

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:16.649
He was tough old-school style

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:18.951
In my house, if you did wrong

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:21.620
Let him rest in peace, dad died too young

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.888
You got the strap

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:23.589
Yeah

00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:25.424
Okay?

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:26.359
Oh, yeah

00:10:26.359 --> 00:10:29.428
And if you saw that belt come out, you ran for cover

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:33.199
If you look above that blue yawning

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:34.533
Well, that's where the restaurant was

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:36.235
and that apartment window right there

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:37.436
with the air conditioner

00:10:37.436 --> 00:10:39.705
is where Joe Pesci lived

00:10:40.873 --> 00:10:41.807
Before he was famous?

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:42.508
Yeah

00:10:44.644 --> 00:10:48.047
So, a lot of our big Italian-American stars

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:49.081
grew out of this neighborhood?

00:10:49.081 --> 00:10:51.384
Yes, some of them are Chas Palmatary, Joe Pesci

00:10:51.384 --> 00:10:54.053
spent a great part of his youth here

00:10:54.053 --> 00:10:57.156
Sicilian, Calabria, and Naples

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:58.557
Same with me!

00:10:58.557 --> 00:10:59.325
Seriously

00:10:59.325 --> 00:11:00.126
It's a crazy combo

00:11:00.126 --> 00:11:01.627
Seriously, seriously. Yeah

00:11:01.827 --> 00:11:04.463
So, that's classified Italian American

00:11:04.463 --> 00:11:05.264
Yeah

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:07.299
You don't call yourself Italian

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:08.534
though you are

00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:09.802
but you're an American

00:11:09.802 --> 00:11:11.804
You're born here. An Italian American

00:11:11.804 --> 00:11:15.207
How many generations do you think that can go back?

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:21.714
Cus my DNA comes from that part of the world

00:11:21.714 --> 00:11:24.417
I can't claim I'm Italian but I tell you

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.752
Italian food does bring about warmth

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:28.287
We always had pastas every Sunday

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:31.924
like made in my grandmother's pot, you know?

00:11:31.924 --> 00:11:35.361
Sunday dinner just like they did in Italy

00:11:35.361 --> 00:11:38.497
Three o'clock, it was on the table

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:40.232
It was a festival in my house

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:40.966
It was big, yeah

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:42.701
Did yours always end in argument and conflict?

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:43.903
All the time

00:11:43.903 --> 00:11:44.303
Okay

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:45.571
Ours did too

00:11:45.571 --> 00:11:48.674
It wasn't just Sundays, it was holidays

00:11:48.674 --> 00:11:51.610
That's just a part of how we are

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.778
What is that?

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:54.714
Highly emotional, right?

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.682
There's an expression coming out of Naples

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:59.685
in a tank or you go "a fanabla"

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:02.421
If you said “a fanabla" that's a curse

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:03.756
and you better run

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:07.827
But here's Arthur Avenue which hasn't changed

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:11.363
Except for a few... like the hair salons

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:12.231
Few stores

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:17.036
Stickball, spongeball, kickball, uhh...

00:12:17.036 --> 00:12:19.238
Johnny on a pony

00:12:22.808 --> 00:12:25.344
ping pong against the wall with a sponge

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:28.347
with a spolding ball, spades they called it

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:30.983
Scully in the street with the caps we used to take

00:12:30.983 --> 00:12:32.017
I don't know what that is

00:12:32.017 --> 00:12:35.354
Well, what we did is we used to go to the cars

