00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:42.087
24/7. That was our hangout

00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:43.422
There's a lot of beer drinking

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:45.757
A lot of parties, a lot of fun

00:23:45.757 --> 00:23:47.159
Grew up with all of them

00:23:47.159 --> 00:23:50.061
A lot of them are not around no more

00:23:50.061 --> 00:23:52.631
It was great growing up before the internet, huh?

00:23:52.631 --> 00:23:54.366
Oh, yeah

00:23:54.366 --> 00:23:56.835
We have one guy named Slim, Willie Rodriguez

00:23:56.835 --> 00:23:58.737
Williams, he was Latino

00:23:58.737 --> 00:24:01.406
In this neighborhood that got along with every Italian

00:24:01.406 --> 00:24:04.543
From the merchant to the old people

00:24:04.543 --> 00:24:07.579
He was such a helpful, caring young guy

00:24:07.579 --> 00:24:08.914
Will he die too young

00:24:08.914 --> 00:24:11.416
Slim, we called him Slim

00:24:11.416 --> 00:24:12.551
And he ran that club

00:24:12.551 --> 00:24:14.319
He made sure the dues were paid

00:24:14.319 --> 00:24:15.287
He lived in there

00:24:15.287 --> 00:24:17.422
And he he passed away in his sleep

00:24:17.422 --> 00:24:19.758
And I took that bad cus he was one

00:24:19.758 --> 00:24:23.562
of my one of my best, you know?

00:24:23.562 --> 00:24:24.830
It's Catania's

00:24:24.830 --> 00:24:25.797
You wanna get a slice?

00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:27.299
Yeah, let's check this out

00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:31.236
Let me throw that away

00:24:35.207 --> 00:24:36.541
Don’t put that on camera 

00:24:36.541 --> 00:24:38.143
cus my doctor don't wanna see that

00:24:38.143 --> 00:24:39.144
Oh, the cigarette?

00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:41.847
What am I gonna do? You were smoking, Rich

00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:43.148
Well, my doctor won't see it

00:24:43.148 --> 00:24:44.716
Yeah, he won't see it

00:24:46.818 --> 00:24:48.520
What's going on here? Catania’s pizza

00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:49.888
We grew up with him and his brother

00:24:49.888 --> 00:24:52.524
Hi to you too

00:24:52.524 --> 00:24:53.358
I didn't see you

00:24:53.358 --> 00:24:55.060
What do you mean you didn’t f**king see me

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:55.760
 I’m right here!

00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:57.762
My vision has gotten worse

00:24:57.762 --> 00:25:00.532
You've got older and I got older

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:02.500
Your vision’s gotten worse?

00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:04.502
I'll do a slice of cheese pizza

00:25:04.502 --> 00:25:06.905
A lot more than your vision's gotten worse

00:25:06.905 --> 00:25:08.006
A lot

00:25:08.006 --> 00:25:10.208
Now, I still write and do my thing though

00:25:10.208 --> 00:25:12.677
I don't get over here as much as I'd like to

00:25:12.677 --> 00:25:15.013
You used to get here a lot more often

00:25:15.013 --> 00:25:16.181
Yeah, I’m busy

00:25:16.181 --> 00:25:17.382
How do you guys feel with Rich

00:25:17.382 --> 00:25:19.518
leaving the neighborhood?

00:25:19.518 --> 00:25:21.186
The neighborhood went to sh*t after he left

00:25:21.186 --> 00:25:21.920
You miss him?

00:25:21.920 --> 00:25:23.355
Yeah, we do miss him

00:25:23.355 --> 00:25:25.657
his sarcasm

00:25:25.657 --> 00:25:27.893
They’re Yankee fans

00:25:27.893 --> 00:25:30.528
Their calzones, you can't beat them

00:25:30.528 --> 00:25:31.429
Can't beat their calzones?

00:25:31.429 --> 00:25:32.330
Are you guys brothers?

00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:32.898
Yes

00:25:32.898 --> 00:25:33.531
Alright

00:25:33.531 --> 00:25:35.166
Rich’s got a great sense of humor 

00:25:35.166 --> 00:25:35.734
He does

00:25:35.734 --> 00:25:36.735
Yeah, I'm liking it

00:25:36.735 --> 00:25:37.903
They don’t make no more

00:25:37.903 --> 00:25:39.137
What about you?

00:25:39.137 --> 00:25:40.972
Not me, I ain’t not funny at all

00:25:41.740 --> 00:25:43.708
I only look funny

00:25:44.509 --> 00:25:47.479
So guys, tell me you're Italian American?

00:25:47.479 --> 00:25:51.049
Yes, Italian American. Born in Italy

00:25:51.049 --> 00:25:52.183
Where?

00:25:52.183 --> 00:25:52.951
Calabria

00:25:52.951 --> 00:25:57.289
Good pizza, straight forward New York pizza

00:25:57.289 --> 00:26:00.592
Little crisp at the bottom

00:26:00.592 --> 00:26:01.726
Good amount of cheese

00:26:05.630 --> 00:26:06.531
Very nice

00:26:06.531 --> 00:26:11.670
This is the mini calzone

00:26:11.670 --> 00:26:15.674
that you could only get at Catania’s

00:26:15.674 --> 00:26:20.512
When we're growing up, 10, 12, 13, 14 years old

00:26:20.512 --> 00:26:22.948
After school, you dropped your books home

00:26:22.948 --> 00:26:24.549
You did a little homework that you got

00:26:24.549 --> 00:26:26.952
And you went out and you played

00:26:26.952 --> 00:26:30.755
5:00-5:30 pm there was

00:26:30.755 --> 00:26:33.325
a bunch of whistles going off

00:26:33.325 --> 00:26:38.596
And every kid knew which whistle was theirs

00:26:38.596 --> 00:26:40.231
That meant dinner time

00:26:40.231 --> 00:26:42.334
Every every parent had a different whistle?

00:26:42.334 --> 00:26:44.336
Everyone had a different whistle

00:26:44.336 --> 00:26:45.604
From the window

00:26:45.604 --> 00:26:48.606
And between 5 and 5:30 pm

00:26:48.606 --> 00:26:51.543
every kid was at the dinner, eating dinner

00:26:51.543 --> 00:26:53.478
Dinner 7 nights a week?

00:26:53.478 --> 00:26:55.413
Every night

00:26:55.413 --> 00:26:57.048
Sundays it was like 1 o’clock

00:26:57.048 --> 00:26:59.084
3 o’clock, 1 o’clock, we ate at 3

00:26:59.084 --> 00:27:02.988
Right. So, and that's what's missing

00:27:02.988 --> 00:27:03.822
That's what's missing

00:27:03.822 --> 00:27:04.990
In society?

00:27:04.990 --> 00:27:06.057
That’s what’s missing

00:27:06.057 --> 00:27:08.626
Because if you didn't get home at 5:30

00:27:08.626 --> 00:27:10.595
You didn't eat

00:27:10.595 --> 00:27:13.098
You didn't eat, you had to wait til tomorrow

00:27:13.098 --> 00:27:15.700
You had to wait til tomorrow

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:17.402
And that's what's missing

00:27:17.402 --> 00:27:19.471
There's no more discipline at home

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:22.440
We got kicked in the a** plenty of times

00:27:22.440 --> 00:27:26.311
But we stayed together

00:27:26.311 --> 00:27:27.879
It's missing

00:27:27.879 --> 00:27:30.415
So where do you think things are going right now?

00:27:30.415 --> 00:27:31.783
There's no discipline

00:27:31.783 --> 00:27:33.785
These kids are doing whatever they want to do

00:27:33.785 --> 00:27:34.719
Told you

00:27:36.287 --> 00:27:39.157
To be fair older people always said that though

00:27:39.157 --> 00:27:41.026
Every parent always said that, right?

00:27:41.026 --> 00:27:41.660
Absolutely

00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:42.761
But you think this time is different?

00:27:42.761 --> 00:27:44.829
You got in trouble in the street

00:27:44.829 --> 00:27:46.731
growing up here

00:27:46.731 --> 00:27:48.900
and somebody yelled at you

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:50.568
or like another parent

00:27:50.568 --> 00:27:52.537
you did not go home and tell your parents

00:27:52.537 --> 00:27:55.273
that you got yelled at by another parent

00:27:55.273 --> 00:27:57.409
Because if you did, you were wrong

00:27:57.409 --> 00:27:59.310
They yelled at you for a reason

00:27:59.310 --> 00:28:00.745
They didn't yell at you for nothing

00:28:00.745 --> 00:28:03.148
So, everyone's parents

00:28:03.148 --> 00:28:04.716
were looking out for the other kids?

00:28:04.716 --> 00:28:07.085
Absolutely

00:28:07.085 --> 00:28:10.388
That was called community, neighborhood

00:28:10.388 --> 00:28:12.290
which you don't have anymore

00:28:12.290 --> 00:28:13.792
There's no more communities

00:28:13.792 --> 00:28:14.893
There's no more neighborhoods

00:28:14.893 --> 00:28:16.227
There's nothing

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:17.429
Done

00:28:17.429 --> 00:28:20.398
That's depressing, guys

00:28:21.399 --> 00:28:23.101
Now they want the cops to be the community

00:28:23.101 --> 00:28:26.704
Back in the day it was somebody else's parent

00:28:26.704 --> 00:28:28.406
that told you, "Hey, what are you still doing here?

00:28:28.406 --> 00:28:29.407
It's 5:30, don't you think you

00:28:29.407 --> 00:28:30.975
should be home eating?

00:28:30.975 --> 00:28:33.344
If they were out, or coming home from work, or whatever

00:28:33.344 --> 00:28:35.046
There was no homeless

00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:36.815
If you were homeless, you didn't belong in that block

00:28:36.815 --> 00:28:38.650
We had a neighborhood bum, you know?

00:28:38.650 --> 00:28:39.484
Absolutely

00:28:39.484 --> 00:28:40.719
Miguel is still around

00:28:40.719 --> 00:28:42.087
But he didn't sleep on the bench

00:28:42.087 --> 00:28:47.025
Yes, and then we had Ozark

00:28:47.025 --> 00:28:49.394
Remember Pasquale? Yeah. Pasquale

00:28:52.797 --> 00:28:54.165
Remember Pasquale

00:28:54.165 --> 00:28:55.400
My first time in this neighborhood

00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:57.402
it looks pretty good

00:28:57.402 --> 00:29:00.305
It was a lot better. It was so much better

00:29:00.305 --> 00:29:01.740
If you think this is good…

00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:04.275
There was a lot of kids

00:29:04.275 --> 00:29:06.211
Just kids running around the streets and whatnot?

00:29:06.211 --> 00:29:09.681
There was leagues in the neighborhood

00:29:09.681 --> 00:29:11.716
Like for instance the softball league

00:29:11.716 --> 00:29:14.052
There was 6-7 teems

00:29:14.052 --> 00:29:17.222
Each kid was from the neighborhood

00:29:17.222 --> 00:29:18.456
That’s a lot of kids

00:29:18.456 --> 00:29:20.225
Always playing ball. That's a lot of kids

00:29:20.225 --> 00:29:23.228
Basketball league, remember the basketball league?

00:29:23.228 --> 00:29:25.930
Each block had their own team

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:27.799
Now you can't get five kids to play

00:29:27.799 --> 00:29:29.334
basketball, baseball, whatever

00:29:29.334 --> 00:29:30.702
And you competed against this block

00:29:30.702 --> 00:29:33.471
Everybody’s home on their computer, on their phone

00:29:33.471 --> 00:29:34.172
And that's the difference

00:29:34.172 --> 00:29:35.640
We don’t give up

00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:37.642
We fight for our values

00:29:37.642 --> 00:29:39.544
We believe in our culture

00:29:39.544 --> 00:29:41.779
And we're a united people

00:29:41.779 --> 00:29:44.015
We might not have money but we have everything

00:29:44.015 --> 00:29:46.017
You’ve got great food

00:29:46.017 --> 00:29:49.020
You've heard the expression about Italian La Familia

00:29:49.020 --> 00:29:49.988
This is it

00:29:49.988 --> 00:29:51.055
It’s your family

00:29:51.055 --> 00:29:52.757
Like these guys are not friends

00:29:52.757 --> 00:29:54.392
They've been my family for years

00:29:54.392 --> 00:29:56.694
I don't see them every day

00:29:56.694 --> 00:29:58.930
He said it when I walked in here

00:29:58.930 --> 00:30:00.932
I mean, I wish I could see him everyday

00:30:00.932 --> 00:30:04.736
But that's part of that growing up La Familia

00:30:04.736 --> 00:30:06.070
That's it

00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:07.539
You deliver this?

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:09.007
Yeah, I'm gonna deliver it right now

00:30:09.007 --> 00:30:10.208
Where you going?

00:30:10.208 --> 00:30:12.076
I'm going to Adam's place

00:30:12.076 --> 00:30:13.344
You’re just gonna walk it there?

00:30:13.344 --> 00:30:13.811
That's it!

00:30:13.811 --> 00:30:14.646
No Uber Eats?

00:30:14.646 --> 00:30:15.146
Nope

00:30:17.382 --> 00:30:18.416
Take care!

